# ╭───═══◎◎◎═══───
# 🌿 **Packaging ignore — node fragment (the Node ecosystem)**
# Excluded for every Node-based extension: the dependency tree, the source, the test and tooling surfaces, and the TypeScript contracts. JavaScript is never excluded by extension — the shipped bundle itself is JavaScript — only by path or name pattern.
# ╰───═══◎◎◎═══───
#
# node_modules/** — the installed dependency tree; the bundle is self-contained (no-dependencies law).
node_modules/**
# src/** — the source tree; build input, never runtime content.
src/**
# **/*.ts — stray TypeScript outside src (root gulpfile.ts, fixtures); build input.
**/*.ts
# **/*.tsx — the same class for JSX sources.
**/*.tsx
# **/*.test.* — test files of any format; development instruments (extension is not the class).
**/*.test.*
# **/*.spec.* — spec files of any format; development instruments.
**/*.spec.*
# test/** — test trees and fixtures of any format.
test/**
# coverage/** — coverage output; measurement residue.
coverage/**
# out/** — the legacy bundle target directory; organization bundles ship dist/.
out/**
# .vscode-test/** — the downloaded VS Code test runtime; a large binary tree, never a runtime input.
.vscode-test/**
# tsconfig*.json — the compiler contract; build-time input.
tsconfig*.json
# scripts/** — build and tooling scripts of any language (the typed lane ships .ts, native consumers .mjs — the path class covers both without naming either).
scripts/**
# tools/** — repository-local tooling surfaces.
tools/**
# tooling/** — repository-local tooling surfaces (variant spelling).
tooling/**
